      "description": "Watch Real Salt Lake vs FC Dallas highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The MLS delivered a classic encounter this evening as Real Salt Lake and FC Dallas combined for a high-scoring thriller that kept spectators guessing until the very end. It was a game defined by clinical finishing, tactical shifts, and a dramatic conclusion that will be remembered for the rest of the season. Dallas Strike Early in First-Half Blitz On August 20, 2026, the match exploded into life with FC Dallas taking an aggressive stance from the opening whistle. The visitors broke the deadlock in the 17th minute when Joaquin Valiente found the back of the net courtesy of a Ramiro assist. The momentum stayed firmly with Dallas as Petar Musa doubled the lead just three minutes later, finishing off a pinpoint pass from the active Valiente . Real Salt Lake managed to find a lifeline in the 38th minute when Sergi Solans converted a chance created by Diego Luna . However, any hope of a quick comeback before the break was dashed in the 45th minute. Petar Musa secured his brace after another excellent setup by Valiente , leaving the score at 3-1 as the teams headed into the tunnel for halftime. Real Salt Lake Claw Their Way Back The second half saw a rejuvenated home side determined to erase the deficit. In the 50th minute, Morgan Guilavogui pulled one back for the hosts following an assist from Noel Caliskan . The pressure from Real Salt Lake became relentless, and the equalizer finally arrived in the 64th minute. Diego Luna , who had been instrumental all night, turned scorer by finishing a pass from substitute Saba Lobjanidze to make it 3-3. Stoppage Time Heartbreak As the clock ticked into stoppage time, the intensity reached a boiling point with several players receiving yellow cards in the closing stages. In the 91st minute, the decisive blow was struck. Ran Binyamin , having come off the bench, produced a clinical finish from a Ramiro pass to put FC Dallas ahead 4-3. Although Binyamin was cautioned in the aftermath, his goal proved to be the winner as the referee blew the final whistle shortly after, ending a breathless night of football."
